      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "\\[PQ = 9\\] \nThe area of $\\triangle POQ$ is $\\frac{1}{2}x_yQ = \\frac{1}{2}xx_1Y1Function: slash = 30``Y.\n\nTo find the area of triangle POQ, we need to find the coordinates of P and Q.\nSince P lies on the x-axis, it has coordinates (x, 0).\nSince Q lies on the y-axis, it has coordinates (0, y).\nWe are given that the line passes through these points with the slope of 3/4, so we can find the equation of the line:\n\\[y - 0 = \\frac{3}{4}(x - x)\\]\n\\[y = \\frac{3}{4}x + \\frac{3}{4}y\\]\n\\[y - \\frac{3}{4}y = \\frac{3}{4}x - x\\]\n\\[\\frac{1}{4}y = -\\frac{1}{4}x\\]\n\\[y = -x + 9\\]\nTherefore, the line intersects the x-axis at -9 and the y-axis at 9. So, P has coordinates (-9, 0) and Q has coordinates (0, 9). The area of triangle POQ is calculated as follows:\n\\[Area = \\frac{1}{2}ax_yQ = \\frac{1}{2}xx_1Y1Function: slash = 30``Y = \\frac{1}{2}(9)(9) = 45\\]\nNow, since the area of triangle TOP is three times the area of triangle POQ, we have:\n\\[Area_{TOP} = 3 Area_{POQ} = 3(45) = 135\\]\nWe are given that T(r, s) lies on line segment PQ, so its coordinates must satisfy the equation of the line:\n\\[y = -\\frac{3}{4}x + 9\\]\nSolving for s in terms of r:\n\\[s = -\\frac{3}{4}r + 9\\]\n\\[r + s = r - \\frac{3}{4}r + 9 = \\frac{1}{4}r + 9\\]\nSince T lies on line segment PQ, its x-coordinate is non-negative (r >= 0).\nTherefore, the value of r + s is 0 + 9 - \\frac{3}{4}*0 = 9.\nTherefore, the answer is $\\boxed{9}$.",
